This project is built on the architectural model of OpenMausBot
(https://github.com/milind-soni/OpenMausBot), Copyright 2026 Milind Soni and
OpenMausBot contributors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

What was adapted (concepts and schema, reimplemented from scratch, no verbatim
source code copied):

  - The "each bot is a real agent" data model: name, soul (standing
    instructions), private memory, skills, routines, approvalMode, computer,
    and a per-agent bound model engine.  See agents-core.js (DEFAULT_AGENT,
    AgentRegistry, ModelRouter).
  - The Electron desktop security model: contextIsolation on, a single
    whitelisted contextBridge object exposed to the renderer (window.ingrid),
    and no Node/ipcRenderer access from page code.  See main.js / preload.js.
  - The local-first storage principle and bring-your-own-agent approach
    (reusing locally logged-in CLIs instead of bare API keys).

The full Apache License 2.0 text is in LICENSE.

